# p384_language.py frozen. field.in/field.out: std:p384's six-limb Montgomery field and order
# arithmetic (the driver appends the old FIELD_MAIN to stdlib/p384.neo) against Python integers; records
# [order u8][op u8][a 48][b 48] -> 48 bytes (op 0 a*b, 1 a+b, 2 a-b, 3 a^-1, 4 a mod m, 5 a*a).
# p384.in: tests/fixtures/language_p384.neo public-key validation (mode 1, keys.in) and batched ECDSA
# verification (mode 0, ecdsa.in) against Go's crypto/ecdsa (tests/p384_oracle.go): one 1/0 per record.
# 104 public keys (18 valid generated/special keys, malformed and off-curve encodings)
1 0	f:keys.in	0	t:11111111111111111100100000000100000000100000000100000000000000100000000100000000100000000100000000000000
# 1013 ECDSA verifications: Go signatures, high-s, bit flips, wrong keys/messages, r/s range and DER errors
0 0	f:ecdsa.in	0	t:
# mode 2: the first P-384/SHA-384 record twice (the second run alters the message)
2 2	x:	0	t:valid=1\n
